# ── Legacy wraptorstricity.com URLs (WordPress site this will replace) ──
# NOT MAPPED YET. The old-URL → new-URL rules are phase 8 of
# MIGRATION-DOCS/MIGRATION-PLAYBOOK.md and need Tri-City's own inventory
# (TRICITY-DISCOVERY.md) and approval. No rules were copied from another
# location's site, even though the old WordPress URLs look alike.
#
# Conventions (Netlify), for when the rules are added:
# - Every target is the final trailing-slash URL. Pages are prerendered to
#   <route>/index.html, which Netlify serves at /<route>/ and 301s
#   /<route> to, so a slash-less target would add a second hop.
# - Netlify strips the trailing slash before matching, so each rule also
#   covers the slash-less copies the old site served.
# - Static files win over these rules. Old URLs that are real pages on the
#   new site need no rule.
# - Domain variants (bare domain, http) are handled by setting
#   www.wraptorstricity.com as the primary domain in Netlify.

# Every real route the app defines is prerendered to a real static file by
# scripts/prerender.mjs, and static files always take priority over this
# file on Netlify — so this catch-all only fires for a genuinely invalid
# path, and it returns a real 404 rather than the homepage.
/*  /404.html  404
